SUPABASE_URL="https://bglvuclrleoqivyzlmdi.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=""
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""

STELLAR_NETWORK_PASSPHRASE="Test SDF Network ; September 2015"
STELLAR_RPC_URL="https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org"
SEALER_SECRET_KEY=""
SEALER_ALLOWED_ORIGIN="http://localhost:3000"

# The account that pays for moving a phase on when its deadline passes.
#
# It needs funding and nothing else. `advance_phase` asks for no signature, so
# this address holds no authority the public does not hold: anybody could send
# the same call and the contract could not tell the two apart. Its own key
# rather than the sealer's, because the sealer's address is named in the
# constitution and should not also be running errands.
#
# Without it the clock will not start, and phases wait for somebody to press the
# button on the manage page.
CLOCK_SECRET_KEY=""

# How long between laps, in milliseconds. This is the worst case a deadline can
# be late by. Default 120000.
#
# Every lap costs two reads whether or not anything has happened, so this and
# the two below are what a quiet month of hosting actually costs. Shorten them
# for a live event, and put them back afterwards.
CLOCK_EVERY_MS=""

# The same, for the service that publishes the sealed roots. It has to keep up
# with the clock: a root can only be published while the hackathon is judging,
# so a sealer lapping slower than the clock would be left holding scores it can
# no longer put on chain. Default 120000.
SEALER_EVERY_MS=""

# How long the indexer waits when the chain had nothing new, in milliseconds,
# and how long it trusts its list of hackathons between reads. Defaults 60000
# and 300000.
#
# The first of these was five seconds, which on its own spent more egress than
# a free Supabase organization gets in a month. Nothing depends on it being
# short: the contract enforces every deadline, and this only decides how far
# behind the chain a page can be.
INDEXER_IDLE_MS=""
INDEXER_WATCHED_FOR_MS=""

# Which hackathon the indexer follows when the whole backend is started with
# `npm run dev`. It takes one contract at a time, so this is how somebody
# switches between events without editing a command.
#
# Only `npm run dev` reads it. Running the indexer directly still takes the
# address as an argument.
# Narrows the indexer to one hackathon. Left empty it follows every hackathon
# in the database, which is what you want unless you are debugging one event.
WATCH_CONTRACT=""
